  {
    slug: 'homebrew-tap',
    name: 'homebrew-tap',
    kind: 'platform',
    tagline: 'The Homebrew tap that packages the released Knowledge Islands command-line tools.',
    description:
      'A delivery repository, not an ecosystem authority. It implements the release transport that each tool repository owns: a validated formula per released tool, so Homebrew takes responsibility for installation, upgrade, and removal on a user\'s machine. It also fans a verified release event out to the repositories that consume one — this website among them.',
    problem:
      'A curl-to-shell installer is fine once and awkward afterwards: nothing owns the upgrade and nothing owns the removal. The tap gives the released tools a single versioned install surface, so they are installed, upgraded and removed with the same commands as everything else on the machine.',
    audience:
      'You want this if you are installing Knowledge Islands tools on macOS or Linux and would rather Homebrew owned them than a script you ran once and forgot.',
    capabilities: [
      'One validated formula per released tool — currently ki, mgit, rig, git-almanac and techne.',
      'Implicit tapping: naming the tap in the install argument is enough, with no separate tap step.',
      'A verified release event fanned out to the repositories that consume one, this website among them.'
    ],
    state:
      'Published and in use, with five formulae packaged. A formula is bumped when its tool cuts a release, so the tap follows the tools rather than leading them.',
    limits:
